    "canonical_bytes": {
      "$comment": "The three byte encodings the substrate publishes for signal outputs. They are pinned here rather than inferred from a projection because the wire format depends on them directly: a conforming implementation must agree on these bytes for any signal whose output has one of these shapes, including signals it defines itself. `bool` had no vector anywhere until 2026-10-09 and no shipped signal produces it, so an implementation encoding `true` as 0xFF would have passed every other case in this file.",
