    "composites": {
      "$comment": "The composite rule of `docs/SPEC.md` \u00a74.4: the \u00a74.2 fold with the caller's own already-lifted distinctions as the alphabet. Every element is *derived* rather than listed \u2014 `{tip_of_byte: n}` is the tip in `lift.tips`, and `{case: name}` is the result of an earlier case here \u2014 so no value in this block is written down twice and none can be copied in wrong. The anchor is `d` from `projections.history` unless a case names a domain. The pair that matters is `flat_1_2_3` against `nested_1_2_then_3`: same leaves, same order, different grouping, so an implementation that flattens structure disagrees with them while reproducing every other value in this file.",
