    "engine_state": {
      "$comment": "What constructing the byte alphabet does to an engine, which is the only way to check \u00a74.3's rule that every lift step is witnessed. Two implementations can agree on every other value in this file and differ here by an order of magnitude, because no projection case follows a lift: one that materialises the 256 tips through the engine reaches 513 distinctions, one that computes them privately reaches 41 after a two-byte fold. Found by an implementation written from docs/SPEC.md alone, which took the second reading.",
