        "canonical_bytes": ""
      },
      {
        "$comment": "Pins HopDistance as the SHORTEST path rather than first-visit order. Rooted at d0, where d1 sits at distance 2 via c and also on a longer route d0 -> d -> e -> d1 of length 3; an implementation that records the first route a traversal happens to take reports 3. The eighteen cross-product cases are all rooted at c, where no node is reachable at two different distances, so none of them can tell the two rules apart. Found by an implementation written from docs/SPEC.md alone, which chose correctly and said the fixture would not have caught it.",
