  "reject": {
    "$comment": [
      "The trust boundary is REJECTION semantics, and a fixture of values to",
      "reproduce cannot express it. Without this section, 'conforming' means",
      "'agrees on good input' \u2014 and an implementation that accepts a",
      "well-formed forgery passes the rest of this suite perfectly.",
      "",
      "Each case is the valid adjacency_upstream_hops2 wire form with one",
      "thing wrong, so a failure localises to the check that is missing.",
      "`expect.kind` names the error class; `offset` and `reason` are given",
      "where the specification fixes them. `any_rejection` means the input",
      "must be refused but the specification does not fix which error.",
      "",
      "Restoring is verification, not deserialisation: a restored projection",
      "is re-materialised from the receiver's own state and compared.",
      "",
      "Note on `any_rejection`: for a truncation, which check fires depends on where the shift lands, so the specification fixes only that the input is refused. Demanding a particular error there would fail a conforming implementation \u2014 this was found by the suite doing exactly that."
    ],
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "bad_magic",
        "why": "First four bytes are not ASCII KPRJ. An implementation that skips the magic will happily decode anything of the right length.",
        "bytes": "",
        "expect": {
          "kind": "Malformed",
          "offset": 0,
          "reason": "bad magic"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "unsupported_version",
        "why": "Version byte is not 0x02. A future wire format must be refused, not guessed at.",
        "bytes": "",
        "expect": {
          "kind": "Malformed",
          "offset": 4,
          "reason": "unsupported version"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "unknown_boundary_tag",
        "why": "Boundary tag outside {0x00 hops, 0x01 saturated}. 0x02 is reserved and withheld, so accepting it would admit an order-bearing read the substrate cannot honour.",
        "bytes": "",
        "expect": {
          "kind": "Malformed",
          "offset": 21,
          "reason": "unknown boundary tag"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "unknown_direction_tag",
        "why": "Direction tag outside {0x00 upstream, 0x01 downstream, 0x02 undirected}.",
        "bytes": "",
        "expect": {
          "kind": "Malformed",
          "offset": 30,
          "reason": "unknown direction tag"
        }
      },
      {
